WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.210
Track it right, test it fairly, launch it safely.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.910
This is the video for module two of Paid Advertising with Meta Ads.

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:22.130
Most failed campaigns are not killed by bad ads. They are killed by bad set-up: an ad account owned by someone who left, a Pixel that fires Purchase twice, or a card declined on day three.

4
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:28.630
This module builds the foundation properly, so the numbers you optimise on are real.

5
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:40.310
The business owner should own the business portfolio, the ad account and the Pixel. You are added as a partner, never given their password, and if you leave they keep everything.

6
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:52.760
Turn on two-factor authentication for everyone, with two trusted admins. Test the payment method, verify the Pixel and the domain, and set an account spending limit as a safety net.

7
00:00:54.010 --> 00:01:05.680
The Meta Pixel is a small piece of code that sends events, like add to cart or purchase, to Meta. Open Test events, then browse your site. Each event should appear within seconds.

8
00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:14.630
Check each page with the free Meta Pixel Helper on a laptop. Then place a real low-value test order and refund it.

9
00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:27.930
Add the Conversions API, which sends the same events from the server and recovers ones the browser misses. Both must carry the same event ID, so Meta removes duplicates.

10
00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:44.110
Halima's shop showed 40 purchases in Ads Manager, but only 22 real paid orders. Purchase was firing twice. After the fix, ROAS fell from an inflated 5.6 to a true 3.05.

11
00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:53.540
Custom audiences are people who already know you. Retarget people who added to cart in the last 14 days but did not buy.

12
00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:59.760
And exclude existing customers, so you stop paying to show them first-order offers.

13
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:17.280
A lookalike asks Meta to find people who resemble a source. It needs at least 100 people from one country, and your 600 best repeat customers beat 5,000 people who once liked a post. Uploading a customer list needs their consent.

14
00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:28.130
Broad targeting works best once your Pixel has purchase history. But location stays a hard rule. If you only deliver in Lagos, set Lagos.

15
00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:41.800
A test must change one thing only, start with a written hypothesis, have enough budget, and run for a fixed time. Ruth wants to test a demonstration video against a price-led carousel.

16
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:54.930
Purchases cost about 4,000 naira. For 30 per version she needs 60, which is 240,000 naira, about 17,100 a day over 14 days.

17
00:02:56.180 --> 00:03:03.220
The client has only 8,000 naira a day. That buys just 14 purchases per version, too few to trust.

18
00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:14.990
So she tests on add to cart instead, at about 900 naira each. That gives roughly 62 per version, then she confirms the winner on purchases later.

19
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:30.900
Read Meta's Advertising Standards for each client. Copy that implies you know something personal, like struggling with your weight, gets rejected. So do guaranteed health or beauty results, get-rich offers and fake buttons.

20
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:45.540
Write: our programme helps people who. Keep claims honest, with NAFDAC registration where a product needs it. If it is a real breach, fix it, because repeated violations can restrict the whole ad account.

21
00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:56.180
Run your pre-launch check on a phone every time. Then in the first hours, check only for faults: is it delivering, is spend on track, any rejections?

22
00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:10.120
Leave it alone during learning. From day 7, compare each ad set with your target cost per sale. Watch for creative fatigue: frequency climbing while clicks fall. The fix is new creative.

23
00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:25.790
When an ad set beats target, raise its budget in modest steps, not double. Write every change in a change log, with the date and reason, and send a plain weekly report that leads with orders, revenue and cost per order.

24
00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:42.000
To remember. The client owns every asset. Verify that Purchase fires once. Use custom audiences to retarget and exclude. Test one variable with enough events. And check every launch on a phone, and log every change.

25
00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:59.530
Now practise. Set up and verify a Pixel on a practice site and record what fires. Design an audience and test plan with a budget calculation. Then build your reusable QA checklist, naming system, change log and report template.

26
00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.820
Continue with the lessons below.
